\section inst_overview Overview

This document describes how to build and use %ObjectHandler from an official
release of the source code.  Two builds are supported:

\li the <b>Visual Studio</b> solution file, which runs on Windows and builds the
C++ libraries and the Excel components; and
\li the <b>cmake</b> build, which runs on Windows and on POSIX systems such as
Linux.  On POSIX systems it builds the C++ library; on Windows it additionally
builds the Excel components.

%ObjectHandler logging is performed by the C++ standard streaming library.

Some %ObjectHandler source code is generated by the
<a href="http://www.gensrc.org">gensrc</a> utility.

The source code is distributed as a single archive that bundles %ObjectHandler
together with gensrc and the other projects in the distribution.  It is
available from the
<a href="https://github.com/eehlers/QuantLibAddIn">QuantLibAddin</a> repo.

No binary installer is provided for the standalone %ObjectHandler library.
However %ObjectHandler functionality is compiled into the binary
installation of <a href="http://www.quantlibxl.org">QuantLibXL</a>.

